  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "How a finding is judged",
      "items": [
        "A finding carries severity (blocker · warn · nit), a lens and a summary; section, line and fix are optional",
        "A blocker is one of four: a declared gate, contract or prompt is violated; a legal input escapes the declared failure face; the gate fails or the suite can never go red; a security or privacy defect",
        "Debt inside the contract is a warn — a duplicated policy, a stale docstring, a missing coverage case; style and naming are a nit",
        "The reviewed artifact is a vision, not an enumeration — its silence is not permission, and the grade judges what a reasonable reader expects",
        "Before the verdict: list every behavior set aside as out of scope, one line each, and acknowledge what was done well"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "One-way fix, one closure",
      "items": [
        "The review's findings decide the route: any finding → fix; zero findings → close now",
        "The fix answers every finding with a disposition — it never authors a verdict of its own",
        "After the fix: a blocker left → re-review; warn/nit only → REVIEW_FIX closure, no re-review",
        "50 consecutive blocker cycles reaches the soft cap: the run defers to the user instead of looping unseen"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "The terminal verdict",
      "items": [
        "Every dispatched round books a record — the pre-dispatch HEAD as its baseline, a verdict { treeClean, targetAction }, the graded violations and the carrier path",
        "A blocked or timed-out round books a record too, so \"the round did nothing\" is never a silent absence",
        "Completion is a criterion per verb, never the child's exit code: implement owes a commit since the group baseline, review an approving carrier, fix a disposition per finding",
        "The persisted completion counter is gone — the count derives from the records, and the tree observation rides the verdict"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "The next: contract",
      "items": [
        "The next: line and the reason line that follows it are the last two lines of a run — the route and its cause; a BLOCKED or TIMEOUT round carries neither",
        "One derivation answers the hop, and the board renders that same judgment — the line and the board cannot disagree",
        "Pipeline handoff: phase-spec → cdd-plan · plan → cdd-dev · wave → branch review · branch → cdd-close · overall → done",
        "A plan revision reopens a closed branch line, so the re-review judges the plan the branch review actually bound"
      ]
    }
  ]
